1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,688
This is AivaCare, an agentic AI platform for continuous care of fatty liver disease,

2
00:00:05,738 --> 00:00:08,984
built as a working prototype for LiverWell Clinic.

3
00:00:09,034 --> 00:00:14,192
In the next five minutes, I'll show what we built, how it works under the hood,

4
00:00:14,242 --> 00:00:17,686
and the experience from each persona's point of view.

5
00:00:18,636 --> 00:00:23,613
Today, patients like John Miller, forty-eight, with fatty liver disease,

6
00:00:23,663 --> 00:00:26,545
see their hepatologist every three months.

7
00:00:26,595 --> 00:00:28,779
Between visits, his lab results,

8
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:35,412
medical records and Apple Watch data sit in separate systems, and nobody is watching the trend.

9
00:00:35,462 --> 00:00:37,925
Concerning changes are noticed late.

10
00:00:37,975 --> 00:00:44,069
AivaCare moves the clinic to continuous care: monitor between visits, guide the patient,

11
00:00:44,119 --> 00:00:49,235
and bring the right findings to the care team, with physicians in control.

12
00:00:50,185 --> 00:00:56,419
We built three entry points on one platform: a patient mobile app, a patient web portal,

13
00:00:56,469 --> 00:01:01,131
and a clinician care dashboard, plus presenter controls for demos.

14
00:01:01,181 --> 00:01:07,415
It runs on Google Cloud with synthetic data, uses a FHIR record as the system of record,

15
00:01:07,465 --> 00:01:09,271
and uses Claude as the AI.

16
00:01:10,221 --> 00:01:16,577
Under the hood, the principle is simple: rules decide, AI explains, physicians approve.

17
00:01:16,627 --> 00:01:20,994
A deterministic rules engine watches labs and wearable data,

18
00:01:21,044 --> 00:01:23,719
for example a FIB-4 score above 2.67.

19
00:01:23,769 --> 00:01:29,904
Two Claude agents handle conversation: a Patient Care Agent and a Clinician Copilot.

20
00:01:29,954 --> 00:01:36,088
They reach data only through governed MCP tool servers, bound to the signed-in user.

21
00:01:36,138 --> 00:01:41,610
Guidance comes from clinician-approved content through RAG, with citations.

22
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:47,869
And a LangGraph workflow manages each escalation, pausing until a physician approves.

23
00:01:48,819 --> 00:01:50,358
Let's start with John.

24
00:01:50,408 --> 00:01:56,280
His home page combines lab results from the clinic with daily data from his watch.

25
00:01:56,330 --> 00:02:00,251
His ALT came down from 82 to 44, but it's rising again,

26
00:02:00,301 --> 00:02:03,573
while his weight creeps up and his steps fall.

27
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:06,895
His FIB-4 score is still in the low-risk band.

28
00:02:07,845 --> 00:02:12,473
John asks the assistant: why is my ALT high, and what should I eat?

29
00:02:12,523 --> 00:02:17,849
Watch the steps: it checks his trend data and searches the approved guidance.

30
00:02:17,899 --> 00:02:23,714
The answer quotes his exact values, and each recommendation cites a LiverWell guide,

31
00:02:23,764 --> 00:02:26,786
so John only gets clinician-approved advice.

32
00:02:27,736 --> 00:02:30,067
John can also upload a lab report.

33
00:02:30,117 --> 00:02:35,529
Claude reads the PDF, extracts each result with its units and reference range,

34
00:02:35,579 --> 00:02:37,770
and the platform validates them.

35
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:41,971
John confirms the values before they're saved to his record,

36
00:02:42,021 --> 00:02:44,562
with provenance back to the document.

37
00:02:45,512 --> 00:02:48,844
Now, new results arrive from the lab feed.

38
00:02:48,894 --> 00:02:54,482
The rules engine calculates a FIB-4 of 2.87, above the 2.67 threshold,

39
00:02:54,532 --> 00:03:01,649
and a high-priority alert appears live in the care team's queue, with a 24-hour deadline.

40
00:03:01,699 --> 00:03:05,273
Seconds later, the Copilot's review is ready.

41
00:03:06,223 --> 00:03:09,274
Sam, the care coordinator, triages the queue.

42
00:03:09,324 --> 00:03:13,132
Sam sees the full picture and can acknowledge the alert,

43
00:03:13,182 --> 00:03:16,646
but clinical decisions are reserved for physicians,

44
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:20,160
so the actions show as awaiting physician approval.

45
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:24,055
Doctor Patel opens the Patient 360 view.

46
00:03:24,105 --> 00:03:29,296
She sees the rule evidence, the trends, and the AI review: a headline,

47
00:03:29,346 --> 00:03:34,912
findings with exact values, and citations to the clinic's fibrosis pathway.

48
00:03:34,962 --> 00:03:39,255
She asks the Copilot what changed in the last ninety days.

49
00:03:39,305 --> 00:03:45,095
It pulls the record through governed tools, and answers with dates and values.

50
00:03:46,045 --> 00:03:49,571
The proposed care-plan actions are only drafts.

51
00:03:49,621 --> 00:03:55,659
Doctor Patel removes one, adds a repeat liver panel in four weeks, and approves.

52
00:03:55,709 --> 00:04:01,213
Only now does anything change: the care plan is updated, the task closes,

53
00:04:01,263 --> 00:04:03,192
and every step is audited.

54
00:04:04,142 --> 00:04:09,969
Back on John's phone, a plain-language follow-up from his care team has already arrived,

55
00:04:10,019 --> 00:04:12,640
and his care plan shows the new actions.

56
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,950
Safety comes first.

57
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:21,997
When John writes, my eyes look yellow today, the red-flag guardrail bypasses the AI completely.

58
00:04:22,047 --> 00:04:28,822
He gets urgent-care instructions instantly, and a high-priority alert goes to the care team.

59
00:04:29,772 --> 00:04:34,071
For governance, clinicians can review the versioned rule catalog,

60
00:04:34,121 --> 00:04:38,220
and a full audit trail of every alert, AI review and decision.

61
00:04:39,170 --> 00:04:44,228
That's AivaCare: continuous monitoring, grounded AI support for patients,

62
00:04:44,278 --> 00:04:49,475
and AI-assisted, physician-approved interventions, built on open standards.

63
00:04:49,525 --> 00:04:53,814
The next steps are clinical sign-off of the rules and content,

64
00:04:53,864 --> 00:04:59,831
integration with the clinic's EMR and lab feeds, and a pilot with consenting patients.
